  "text": "Press Releases | NCSBE\nSkip to main content\nThe General Election is Nov. 3\nCheck Your Voter Registration:\nUse the Voter Search Tool\nDid you recently receive a letter about your voter registration?\nFind answers to your questions in our FAQ.\nRead More\nRegistration Repair Project\nCheck if your N.C. voter registration is incomplete, learn how to fix it, and find more information in the FAQ:\nRegistration Repair\nPrevious\nPause\nPlay\nNext\nAn official website of the State of North Carolina\nAn official website of NC\nHow you know\nState Government websites value user privacy. To learn more,\nview our full privacy policy\n.\nSecure websites use HTTPS certificates. A lock icon or https:// means you\u2019ve safely connected to the official website.\nUtility Menu\nAbout\nContact\nMedia\nnc.gov\nMain menu\nRegistering\nRegistering\nHow to Register\nWho Can Register\nUpdating Registration\nChecking Your Registration\nChoosing Your Party Affiliation\nHosting Voter Registration Drives\nNational Voter Registration Act (NVRA)\nFAQ: Voter Registration\nVoting\nVoting\nUpcoming Election\nYour Voter Record\nVoter ID\nVote Early in Person\nVote in Person on Election Day\nVote By Mail\nMilitary and Overseas Voting\nHelp for Voters with Disabilities\nProvisional Voting\nVoter Tools & Forms\nVoting Technology\nVote in Honor of a Veteran\nFor Candidates\nFor Candidates\nRunning for Office\nFiling for Candidacy\nTerms of Office\nCandidate Challenges\nWithdrawal of Candidacy\nPetitions\nResults & Data\nResults & Data\nElection Results\nVoter Registration Data\nCandidate Lists\nAbsentee and Provisional Data\nVoter Turnout\nPolling Place Data\nVoter History Data\nVoting Maps/Redistricting\nCampaign Finance\nCampaign Finance\nRequest for Proposals\nSearch Campaign Funding and Spending Reports\nReporting Schedules\nTreasurer Training\nReporting Software\nReporting Forms\nCandidate Committees\nOther Political Committees\nFederal Political Committees\nIndependent Expenditures, Electioneering Communications and Special Contributors\nReferendum Committees\nLimitation on Fund-Raising During Legislative Session\nDisclosure Legends\nCampaign Finance Audits and Investigations\nPenalties\nCampaign Finance Advisory Opinions\nAbout Elections\nAbout Elections\nCounty Boards of Elections\nElection Security\nLegal Resources\nMaintaining Accurate Voter Rolls\nGet Involved in Elections\nTypes of Elections\nElectoral College\nCareers in Elections\nUtility Menu\nAbout\nContact\nMedia\nnc.gov\nSearch\nHome\nPress Releases\nPress Release Terms\n- Any -\nBoard decisions\nCandidate filing\nCOVID-19\nEarly voting\nElection results\nHearings\nLaws/litigation\nMeeting notices\nPolling places\nPublic comments\nRequired by law\nRulemaking process\nStatements\nVote by mail\nVoter ID information\nSearch\nFact: In NC, Election Workers Often Do Have to Write on Your Ballot\nWed, Oct 14, 2026\nElection workers write on ballots for different reasons as required by law. This in no way affects whether your ballot will be counted.\nElection Officials to Host Media Availability for the Start of Early Voting\nWed, Oct 14, 2026\nNCSBE to Send Letter to Potential Non-Citizens on Voter Rolls\nTue, Oct 13, 2026\nThe North Carolina State Board of Elections will send letters this week to 1,392 registered voters identified as potential non-U.S. citizens through the federal Systematic Alien Verification for Entitlements (SAVE) database.\n10 Things for In-person Early Voters to Know in North Carolina\nFri, Oct 9, 2026\nState Board Meeting (Oct. 8, 2026)\nMon, Oct 5, 2026\nRegular Voter Registration Deadline Approaching for 2026 General Election\nFri, Oct 2, 2026\nExecutive Director Sam Hayes Issues Statement on U.S. Supreme Court Ruling on SAVE Database\nFri, Sep 25, 2026\nPublic Comment Period Set to Begin for Periodic Review of Election Rules\nFri, Sep 18, 2026\nThe State Board of Elections invites members of the public to comment on the State Board\u2019s initial determination that nearly 30 existing administrative rules are still necessary.\nGet Ready to Vote: Tuesday is National Voter Registration Day\nTue, Sep 15, 2026\nTuesday, September 15 is National Voter Registration Day.\nPublic Comment Period to Open for Proposed Rules Regarding Exempt Sales Plans\nMon, Sep 14, 2026\nThe public comment period opens on Tuesday, Sept. 15 and closes at 11:59 p.m. on Monday, Nov. 16, 2026.\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\n9\n\u2026\n\u203a\u203a\nNext page\nLast \u00bb\nLast page\nContact\nNorth Carolina State Board of Elections (NCSBE)\nP.O. Box 27255\nRaleigh, NC 27611-7255\nEmail:\nelections.sboe@ncsbe.gov\nPhone:\n(919) 814-0700\nFax: (919) 715-0135\nFollow Us\nFacebook Posts\nNC State Board of Elections\nCounty Boards Resources\nResources for County Boards\nNCSBE Public Files (FTP)\nVoter Tools\nVoter Search\nCounty Boards of Elections Search\nBallotTrax (Absentee Ballot Tracking)\nVoter Registration Statistics\nView all tools and forms\nWork With Us\nCareer Opportunities\nVoter Information\nUse of Partial Social Security Numbers\nNetwork Menu\nnc.gov\nWebsite Feedback\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & Terms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nOpen Budget\nHosted on Digital Commons",
